From f8da5b3e768151251188f108d86fbd7dc51803c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "mathorax.com" <mathorax1@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:00:53 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add OCR retry, review sheet, and owner corrections

Retry only items held for OCR quality: enhance the cropped image at
about 3x (or raster a PDF page at 350 dpi when there is no image),
then rerun both fidelity OCR passes. Export only if the same strict
gate still passes. Settings live in config/ocr.json under retry.
Every attempt is logged in export/ocr-retry.json.

Still-held items are written to a review sheet (JSON, markdown, and
HTML) with image path, OCR text, PDF text, hold reason, and empty
owner_text / owner_decision fields that are never auto-filled.

A committed review/owner-corrections.json is read on the next run.
Complete corrections (owner_decision plus a structured stem) are
exported as owner_checked, with who, when, and the image sha256, and
still must pass schema and type rules.
