 # Changelog
 
+## Unreleased (local branch feat/ocr-retry-review)
+
+Automatic OCR retry for items held only for OCR quality: re-render the cropped image at about 3x (or raster a PDF page at 300-400 dpi when there is no image), enhance (grayscale, sharpen, contrast), and rerun both fidelity OCR passes. The same strict gate still applies. Settings live in `config/ocr.json` under `retry`. Each attempt is logged in `export/ocr-retry.json`.
+
+Every still-held item is written to `export/review-sheet.json`, `.md` and `.html`, with empty `owner_text` and `owner_decision` fields that are never auto-filled.
+
+A committed `review/owner-corrections.json` is read on the next run. Complete corrections (a filled `owner_decision` plus structured stem, and options or key when needed) are exported as `owner_checked` and still must pass schema and type rules.
+
+Tests: `tests/test_ocr_retry_review.py`.
+
