+
+## Retry block
+
+The `retry` object in `config/ocr.json` controls an automatic second OCR pass for items held only for OCR quality (low word or overall confidence, or disagreeing passes). Type and key holds are not retried.
+
+Default settings:
+
+- `enabled`: true
+- `dpi`: 350 (used when a PDF page is rasterised because the item has no cropped image)
+- `scale`: 3 (used on existing cropped question images)
+- `grayscale`, `sharpen`, `clahe`: true
+- `contrast`: 1.5
+- `binarize`: false (optional)
+- `prefer_pdf_raster`: true, but only when the item has no source images
+- `pdf_enhance_scale`: 1 (do not scale a high-dpi raster again)
+
+The retry writes enhanced images under `out/media/retry`, reruns both fidelity OCR passes, and exports the item only if the same strict gate passes (100 percent word coverage, passes agree, per-word 90, overall 95). Every attempt and outcome is written to `export/ocr-retry.json`.
+
+Items that are still held after the retry (and any other hold) are written to a review sheet: `export/review-sheet.json`, `export/review-sheet.md` and `export/review-sheet.html`. Each row has the image path, OCR text, PDF text, hold reason, and empty `owner_text` / `owner_decision` fields. Those fields are never auto-filled.
+
+Owner corrections live in `exams/CODE/review/owner-corrections.json` in raw-exam. The file is copied into the workspace `review/` folder on the next run. A row is applied only when `owner_decision` and a structured `stem` are both non-empty (plus options and `answer_raw` when the type needs them). A bare `owner_text` blob is not parsed. Corrected items are exported with the `owner_checked` tag and a short `answer.source` record (who, when, image sha256). A full record is also written to `export/owner-checked.json`. Schema and type rules still apply. OCR or coverage holds are skipped only for a complete owner correction, because that is the point of the owner review.
+
+See `examples/owner-corrections.example.json`.
+
